{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1772907031,"nonce":"3gI7pIcUByOiW5DT2B8G66YigoE=","title":"session_projects backfill migration 24 used wrong join condition — no rows updated","message":"Migration 24 backfillProjectRepoNames was supposed to fix historical session_projects rows where repo_id stores a branch name (e.g. feature__audit-fixes) instead of the actual repo name (dotfiles).\n\nThe function joined session_projects with sessions WHERE cwd LIKE \"%/worktrees/%\". But sessions store the REPO ROOT as cwd (e.g. /Users/mll/.dotfiles), NOT the worktree path. So the join found zero rows and did nothing.\n\nThe DB still has 15+ rows with branch-name repo_ids. These get filtered by looksLikeWorktreeOrBranchName() in sessions.tsx, causing the project column to show dashes for those sessions.\n\nFix: Migration 25 with corrected backfill logic:\n- Find session_projects rows where repo_id contains __ or matches branch prefix patterns\n- Join with sessions on session_id = id\n- If cwd is a valid path (exists), extract repo name as stripLeadingDot(basename(cwd))\n- Update repo_id and repo_name","files":null}]}